# Universe content · resource fields (on planets and in space)
# researched: earthsci.org "Classification of Mineral Deposits"; TU Clausthal economic geology notes;
#   USGS porphyry copper summary; standard geology for fossil fuels; space-resource summaries
#   (asteroid and comet makeup in content/small-bodies.unt, giants in content/gas-giants.unt)
# The 100 space resources are listed on the public space page.
# Spec: docs/CONTENT-FORMAT.md · wiki/systems/r06-planet.md · wiki/systems/r10-space.md

# ── Made by magma ──

@deposit layered-intrusion
name: Layered intrusion
real: yes
family: magmatic
gives: chromium, platinum, nickel
says: metals settling in layers inside a slowly cooling body of magma

@deposit kimberlite
name: Kimberlite pipe
real: yes
family: magmatic
gives: diamonds
says: a deep volcanic pipe that carried diamonds up from far below

@deposit pegmatite
name: Pegmatite
real: yes
family: magmatic
gives: lithium, rare elements, gem crystals
says: the last, slowest-cooling part of magma, with giant crystals

# ── Made by hot fluids ──

@deposit porphyry
name: Porphyry deposit
real: yes
family: hydrothermal
gives: copper, molybdenum, gold
says: a huge, low-grade body of metal veins around a cooled magma body; the world's main copper source
where: above plates sinking under other plates

@deposit volcanic-sulfide
name: Volcanic massive sulfide
real: yes
family: hydrothermal
gives: copper, zinc, lead
says: metal-rich mounds made by hot vents on the sea floor

@deposit epithermal
name: Epithermal vein
real: yes
family: hydrothermal
gives: gold, silver
says: shallow veins left by hot water near volcanoes

@deposit skarn
name: Skarn
real: yes
family: hydrothermal
gives: tungsten, iron, copper
says: limestone changed by hot fluids from nearby magma

@deposit orogenic-gold
name: Mountain-belt gold
real: yes
family: hydrothermal
gives: gold
says: gold veins formed while mountains are built

# ── Made by water and time ──

@deposit banded-iron
name: Banded iron formation
real: yes
family: sedimentary
gives: iron
says: striped layers of iron laid down in ancient seas when oxygen first appeared; needs the oxygen-maker stage of life

@deposit placer
name: Placer
real: yes
family: sedimentary
gives: gold, diamonds, tin
says: heavy grains washed together by rivers and waves

@deposit evaporite
name: Evaporite
real: yes
family: sedimentary
gives: salt, potash, gypsum
says: minerals left behind when lakes and seas dry up

@deposit sediment-copper
name: Sediment-hosted copper
real: yes
family: sedimentary
gives: copper, cobalt
says: copper carried by salty underground water into buried sediments

@deposit coal
name: Coal seam
real: yes
family: sedimentary
gives: coal
says: buried ancient forests crushed into black rock; needs forests to have lived

@deposit oil-gas
name: Oil and gas reservoir
real: yes
family: sedimentary
gives: oil, natural gas
says: buried ancient sea life cooked by heat and pressure, trapped under rock; needs life to have lived

# ── Made by weather ──

@deposit laterite
name: Laterite
real: yes
family: weathering
gives: nickel, aluminum (bauxite)
says: rock rotted by tropical rain and heat, leaving metals behind

@deposit soil
name: Fertile soil
real: yes
family: weathering
gives: farmland
says: broken rock plus the remains of life; grows food

@field ocean-water
name: Ocean water
real: yes
family: water
gives: water, salt, dissolved metals
where: seas and oceans
says: the biggest field on a wet world; salt and metals are dissolved in it

# ── Fields in space ──

@field asteroid-metal
name: Metal asteroid field
real: yes
gives: iron, nickel, platinum-group metals

@field asteroid-carbon
name: Carbon asteroid field
real: yes
gives: water, carbon, life chemistry

@field asteroid-stony
name: Stony asteroid field
real: yes
gives: silicates, metals

@field ice-field
name: Ice field
real: yes
gives: water, methane, ammonia
where: comets, Kuiper-belt bodies, ice moons, shadowed polar craters

@field regolith
name: Regolith
real: yes
gives: oxygen bound in rock, metals, helium-3
says: the dusty broken surface of airless moons and asteroids; helium-3 builds up in it from the star's wind

@field giant-atmosphere
name: Giant-planet atmosphere
real: yes
gives: hydrogen, helium-3, deuterium
says: skimmed by fuel scoops

@field nebula-gas
name: Nebula gas
real: yes
gives: hydrogen, rare gases

@field ring-ice
name: Ring ice
real: yes
gives: water ice

@field star-matter
name: Star matter
real: hypothetical
gives: hydrogen, helium, heavy elements
says: lifted straight off a star by a very advanced civilization

@field black-hole-energy
name: Black-hole energy
real: hypothetical
gives: energy
says: drawn from a spinning black hole's ergosphere (content/black-holes.unt)

# ── Generator rules ──

@rule deposit-geology
real: rule
says: deposits follow the planet's geology: magma bodies make magmatic deposits, plate edges and volcanoes make hydrothermal ones, seas and rivers make sedimentary ones, tropical weather makes laterites

@rule deposit-life
real: rule
says: some resources need life to have existed first: banded iron needs oxygen makers, coal needs forests, oil and gas need ancient sea life

@rule deposit-tectonics
real: rule
says: planets with plate tectonics make far more ore deposits than stagnant-lid worlds

@rule deposit-depth
real: rule
says: deeper deposits need better mining tech; placers and surface ores come first

@rule field-space
real: rule
says: space fields follow what the bodies are made of (small bodies, giants, nebulas, rings)

@rule field-deplete
real: rule
says: every deposit and field can run out; civilizations that strip them must move on, as the endgame harvest says
